WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.890
- We've got a great show, everybody.

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.800
And it all starts up on our roof.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:04.633
That's right.

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:06.230
We are in beautiful Southern California.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.030
So we are taking advantage of the weather

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.000
and staying even safer during the surge,

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.060
by hosting some of our guests up there,

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.670
we did it with Chris Kattan yesterday

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:14.720
and it was so awesome, it was fun.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.375
It felt like a date,
but cool, I'm into it.

00:00:16.375 --> 00:00:18.380
So let's set it up right now

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.550
for another Interview Alfresco.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.830
Jason, can you give me
like an extra long sting

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:23.760
while I run upstairs?

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.539
Like I'm in heels, like a long-

00:00:26.539 --> 00:00:27.372
(medieval music)

00:00:27.372 --> 00:00:28.205
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:28.205 --> 00:00:29.713
Okay, here we go, here we go.

00:00:30.562 --> 00:00:33.895
(upbeat medieval music)

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:41.423
All right,

00:00:41.423 --> 00:00:42.920
and just like that,
I'm on the roof, y'all.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.790
These guests are very funny.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.990
You've seen one in The
Office and The Hangover

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:50.300
and the other in a few Marvel
Cinematic Universe projects.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.560
Their new show is True
Story with Ed and Randall

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.230
streaming on peacock.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:55.885
It's Ed Helms and Randall Park.

00:00:55.885 --> 00:00:57.140
(Kelly imitates air horn blaring)

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.576
What's up y'all?

00:00:58.576 --> 00:01:01.090
We can't touch, we can't
touch but we can do this.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:01.923
(Kelly, Ed and Randall laughing)

00:01:01.923 --> 00:01:02.756
Have a seat.

00:01:02.756 --> 00:01:03.840
- All right, I love this.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.290
- We have a new thing
we're trying to like,

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.300
keep it even safer.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.520
Like we're outside.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.360
- [Ed] It's terrific.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.357
- [Randall] Yeah.
- [Kelly] Yes, yes.

00:01:09.357 --> 00:01:10.190
- Are this real waters?

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:11.480
- These are, this isn't real water,

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:12.440
there's no real water.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.424
We actually don't have anything for you.

00:01:14.424 --> 00:01:16.054
It's just a really beautiful table.

00:01:16.054 --> 00:01:18.297
We will bring water out now (laughs).

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.710
So we, this is our Cafe Alfresco.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.150
That's what we're calling it.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.180
But how long have you known each other?

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.500
It feels like your chemistry,

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.316
you have known each other forever.

00:01:27.316 --> 00:01:29.099
- We, we were married.

00:01:29.099 --> 00:01:30.260
(Kelly laughs)
- We're twins.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:31.590
We're actually twins.
- You are married?

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.030
- We, yeah.
- We're fraternal twins.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.462
- Twins and married, it's happening.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:38.540
- We were, uh, we were
friends for a long time,

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.700
we lost touch and then we were reunited

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.960
at Beyonce's birthday.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.548
- [Randall] That's right.
- Right.

00:01:44.548 --> 00:01:45.764
- [Randall] That's right.

00:01:45.764 --> 00:01:46.730
- Because that's where we hang out.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:48.110
- [Kelly] Is that a true
story at Beyonce's birthday?

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:51.950
Okay. I was like, you're
so much cooler than me.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:52.783
Wait, what?

00:01:52.783 --> 00:01:53.650
I was like-

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:56.340
- No, the real story is a lot
more fascinating actually.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.531
We like just kind of met
each other here and there.

00:01:59.531 --> 00:02:00.410
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:03.027
- Yeah, and, and can't
even trace the origin.

00:02:03.027 --> 00:02:04.060
It's been a lot of years.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.020
- I love that though.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.240
Well, you have great chemistry.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.073
That's what I love.

00:02:07.073 --> 00:02:08.220
I saw you all recently on the voice,

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.410
on the last season and y'all are so funny.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.640
It's just so yeah, I love it.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:12.473
I love y'all's chemistry.

00:02:12.473 --> 00:02:14.580
But The Office had a huge comeback,

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.700
like this, like the last several years,

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.533
I think has streaming.

00:02:17.533 --> 00:02:19.170
Like everybody, like all those shows

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.740
that maybe were popular years
ago are coming back around.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:22.573
Is that cool?

00:02:22.573 --> 00:02:24.380
To like have a whole new fan base for it?

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:28.310
- It's totally insane and, and,
and mind blowing, honestly,

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:32.370
like there are kids who
weren't even born when,

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.050
when the shows started,

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:35.810
who are now like avid fans

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:38.228
and it's a, it's a thrill.
- 'Cause it's a great show.

00:02:38.228 --> 00:02:40.540
- Yeah, it's totally, totally amazing.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.123
Randall was on The Office.
- [Kelly] I know.

00:02:42.123 --> 00:02:44.410
- I did an episode and it's crazy

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.157
because I think once-
- It's that what you meant?

00:02:46.157 --> 00:02:48.340
That's what I thought, but
it apparently it wasn't.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:52.860
But I did, I did one scene in one episode,

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.970
I was in and out in like a couple hours.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:56.800
That's part, that one scene is probably

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.914
the thing I'm recognized the most for.

00:02:58.914 --> 00:03:00.453
(Kelly and Ed laugh)

00:03:00.453 --> 00:03:02.255
- You know that's how powerful you are.

00:03:02.255 --> 00:03:03.088
(Randall laughs)

00:03:03.088 --> 00:03:06.200
- It makes our show True
Story an Office reunion.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.454
- [Kelly] It does.
- [Randall] That's right.

00:03:07.454 --> 00:03:09.710
- So in The Office you
did a lot of acapella.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.370
And like I mentioned on
the voice you came back

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.203
and you were on the voice

00:03:12.203 --> 00:03:14.110
and I know you kick
John out of your group,

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:16.190
but Blake is now a member
of your acapella group.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.023
- Yeah, of course.

00:03:17.023 --> 00:03:18.390
We have an Ariana, the whole gang,

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:19.223
everybody's in the group.

00:03:19.223 --> 00:03:20.290
- Just not John.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.371
- Except for John.

00:03:21.371 --> 00:03:22.690
(Kelly and Randall laugh)

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:25.960
Yeah, John and I have a,
we've been rivals for decades.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:28.570
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.
- [Randall] Yeah, yeah.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:29.814
- [Kelly] It makes sense.
- Since Beyonce's party.

00:03:29.814 --> 00:03:30.647
- [Kelly] Since Beyonce's party (laughs).

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:33.050
- [Ed] But yeah, I've done-

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:36.510
- Since we have an acapella
off at Beyonce's party.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.041
- Oh, that's right, of course.

00:03:38.041 --> 00:03:38.950
- Did you grow up, though, really like

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:40.869
singing acapella, like in groups?

00:03:40.869 --> 00:03:42.580
- No, not acapella per se, but I was like,

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.461
kind of like a choral nerd.

00:03:44.461 --> 00:03:45.294
- [Kelly] I was too.
- Yeah, okay.

00:03:45.294 --> 00:03:47.049
So like singing all the time.

00:03:47.049 --> 00:03:52.049
My buddy Warren Goodrich
and I sang More Than Words

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:57.510
at a high school pep rally,
which doesn't even sound cool.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.090
I think we thought it was
cool to do that, but it-

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:01.923
- I still think it's cool

00:04:01.923 --> 00:04:03.150
which is why I was the nerd.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.440
- I'm still proud of it.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.590
But I think, I think that
technically it was not cool.

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:09.820
And that's what part, that's
part of what makes me not cool

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.660
is that I don't agree with that.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:13.070
I still think it's cool.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:14.484
- I still think it's cool.

00:04:14.484 --> 00:04:16.670
What, what were your first concerts?

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:19.169
Like your experience since
you love music so much?

00:04:19.169 --> 00:04:20.630
- My first concert,

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:23.290
I was invited to this concert
I abandoned that I didn't-

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:24.160
- You already feel,

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.658
you already feel like a lo-
- I apologize for it.

00:04:25.658 --> 00:04:26.491
(Kelly, Ed and Randall laugh)

00:04:26.491 --> 00:04:28.050
But no, but it is like,

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.180
since you're asking my first concert,

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.950
I was like, yeah, sure, I'll go.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.690
The band was The Hooters.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.352
Does it, do you remember this band?

00:04:35.352 --> 00:04:36.620
- [Kelly] Is it like the
band for the restaurant?

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:37.950
The wings?
- [Ed] No, no, no.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:38.783
Okay.

00:04:38.783 --> 00:04:40.290
Great valid questions.
- [Kelly] Valid.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.870
- But they were like kind of,
they had like a couple of hits

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:46.330
in the late eighties, I think.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.130
And they were touring like small venues

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:49.380
by the time I was in high school

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:52.930
and we went and it was super fun.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.810
And the drummer at one
point threw his drumsticks

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:57.410
into the crowd.

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:58.330
I caught one.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:04:59.390
(Kelly laughs)
- Oh, wow.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:02.930
- I got, I got a drumstick from the cons

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:03.763
from my very first time.

00:05:03.763 --> 00:05:05.500
- You still have it to this day?

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.030
- I probably lost it that night.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.300
I have no idea what happened.
(Kelly and Randall laugh)

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:09.965
- It was precious.

00:05:09.965 --> 00:05:10.798
What was your first-

00:05:10.798 --> 00:05:12.930
- [Randall] My first
concert was very cool.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:13.770
- What was it?

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:17.144
- It was a well, this was
a, I was a kid, Harry Co-

00:05:17.144 --> 00:05:19.810
I just, I decided Harry Connick Jr.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:20.664
- [Kelly] Yeah, oh.

00:05:20.664 --> 00:05:22.080
- But When Harry Met Sally had come out,

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:25.150
I was obsessed with that movie
and the music in the movie

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:27.550
and Harry Connick Jr. did a
big part of the soundtrack.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:28.383
- [Kelly] He's great.

00:05:28.383 --> 00:05:31.260
- And yeah, and I would just
love the soundtrack so much

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:34.340
and me and a friend found
out he was playing in Vegas.

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:37.116
We, we grew up in LA
and I begged my dad to,

00:05:37.116 --> 00:05:38.947
to take us there and-

00:05:38.947 --> 00:05:41.410
- You begged your dad
to take you (laughs).

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:45.510
- And he drove me and my
friend to Vegas and we just.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.640
- Your dad took you to
Vegas to see a show?

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.473
- [Randall] Yeah.

00:05:48.473 --> 00:05:49.306
- You have a cool dad.

00:05:49.306 --> 00:05:50.139
- [Randall] Very cool of him, yeah.

00:05:50.139 --> 00:05:52.840
- Okay, I was like, I just
love that it was usually like,

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:56.520
not like someone that,
usually it's like a pop band,

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.130
like boy, like, oh, I was just looking

00:05:58.130 --> 00:05:58.963
into a different scenario.

00:05:58.963 --> 00:05:59.796
- What you're saying? What
are you trying to say?

00:05:59.796 --> 00:06:01.000
- No, I just mean usually
it was like, you were,

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.139
you had a very sophisticated
musical palette.

00:06:03.139 --> 00:06:04.611
- [Randall] Yeah.
- [Ed] I agree, I agree.

00:06:04.611 --> 00:06:06.083
- I got there, i got that.

00:06:06.083 --> 00:06:07.587
(Randall and Kelly laugh)
- How old were you?

00:06:07.587 --> 00:06:10.310
- Oh gosh, I must say, maybe
like early high school.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:12.150
- I just mean like people would be like,

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.574
can you take me to Janet Jackson?

00:06:13.574 --> 00:06:14.407
Can you take me-

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:17.188
Like and you're like please,
please Harry Connick Jr.

00:06:17.188 --> 00:06:18.230
He's amazing.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:20.510
I just love that, like, as a kid.

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:22.278
- You were like, can we go to the LA Phil?

00:06:22.278 --> 00:06:23.259
(Kelly and Randall laugh)

00:06:23.259 --> 00:06:24.794
- Please, please.

00:06:24.794 --> 00:06:27.990
(Randall laughing drowns out Kelly)

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.194
- I must see it.

00:06:29.194 --> 00:06:30.027
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:30.027 --> 00:06:30.900
I'd love that.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:33.760
- January is national soup month.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.640
I didn't even know all these
things existed before the show,

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.330
but it's fascinating to find
out and I happen to love soup.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:41.480
So everyone knows now that
this is national soup month.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.300
Since we're at our roof cafe,

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.440
we have our favorite soups to share.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.960
So check out this fancy soup tasting flat

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:49.810
of all our favorites.

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:52.240
And tell us about your
favorite before we dive in.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:53.073
What's your favorite?

00:06:53.073 --> 00:06:55.260
- All right, so, this is my favorite.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:57.530
It's Mulligatawny soup.

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:58.363
- [Kelly] That is fancy.

00:06:58.363 --> 00:07:00.300
- Yeah, which is an Indian soup.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:01.666
The reason that I love it is because

00:07:01.666 --> 00:07:04.140
it was on an episode of Seinfeld

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:06.540
and I think it was the soup Nazi episode.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:07.373
- Oh, wait, is this the one

00:07:07.373 --> 00:07:08.817
"No soup for you next time" line is?

00:07:08.817 --> 00:07:09.650
Oh, my God.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:12.260
And I used to work near the
guy that it was based on,

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:14.410
the actual guy, and I went and I was like,

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.890
I got to go get the
Mulligatawny soup there,

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.890
which I think was Kramer's favorite,

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:20.620
and it instantly became my favorite.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:21.620
It's so good.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.640
- Oh my gosh, I love that backstory.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:24.473
- [Ed] Yeah.

00:07:24.473 --> 00:07:26.443
- And now I feel like mine's
not going to be as cool.

00:07:26.443 --> 00:07:30.117
I love French onion soup
just 'cause it tastes good.

00:07:30.117 --> 00:07:32.181
- [Ed] It's good
- Kay, Ed?

00:07:32.181 --> 00:07:33.780
And I don't have like a really cool story

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:36.624
about a French person that
told me about it or anything.

00:07:36.624 --> 00:07:38.220
I just like it.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:39.160
No, I love it.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:39.993
It's the best.

00:07:39.993 --> 00:07:42.441
And I feel like when
you're, you would get this,

00:07:42.441 --> 00:07:44.820
I traveled so much,
especially in my twenties,

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:46.040
like everywhere in the world.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.561
And I feel like always on the menu,

00:07:47.561 --> 00:07:49.918
there would be French
onion soup and it was like,

00:07:49.918 --> 00:07:53.000
in case you just felt like
you didn't want to risk it

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.660
on something maybe, you were
in like Thailand or something,

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:56.630
you're like, I don't know,

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:59.110
I don't, I can't afford to
get sick before the show.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:00.520
So I'd get French onion soup.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:01.353
That's my thing.

00:08:01.353 --> 00:08:02.186
- Amazing.

00:08:02.186 --> 00:08:03.019
- I love French onion soup,

00:08:03.019 --> 00:08:05.010
but my favorite is the Split Pea Soup.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:06.010
- [Kelly] I've never had this.

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:06.843
- Yes.

00:08:06.843 --> 00:08:09.900
I grew up going to Jewish
delis with my family

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:12.210
and I remember one that
we'd always go to an order,

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:13.410
always ordered the split pea.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:16.385
To this day. I live in Studio City

00:08:16.385 --> 00:08:19.800
or Art's Deli shout out
to Art's Deli on Ventura.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.150
I ordered the split pea.

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:24.500
It's my favorite because it looks healthy.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.866
It feels like it could be healthy.

00:08:26.866 --> 00:08:28.070
- [Kelly] It's like not? (laughs)

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.230
- It's probably really bad for you.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:33.032
- It's hardy.
- It's a hardy situation.

00:08:33.032 --> 00:08:34.706
- Yes.
- Okay.

00:08:34.706 --> 00:08:35.539
- It's really good.
- Okay.

00:08:35.539 --> 00:08:37.450
